      {
        "id": 40759,
        "name": "LCinn",
        "username": "LCinn",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lcinn/{size}/2659_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-10-24T12:13:32.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ameena\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/48/1907_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ameena:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Bleh,I move my played cards around so as to keep track of them - usually I may have Ongoings, then Equipment cards. Or maybe ones that do similar things, such as buff damage, which I do in the case of Ra - I have the Staff and erm, that Ongoing that givse him +1 damage together at the \"start\" (ie left-hand side) of the line, then other stuff afterwards.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>well, the order mostly matters for cards that have overlapping automatic triggers (like most villain and environment cards with their start/end of turn triggers). There's no need at all to keep track of the order of cards without automatic triggers (i.e. most hero cards).</p>",
