      {
        "id": 40760,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-10-24T12:28:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ameena\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/48/1907_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ameena:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Bleh,I move my played cards around so as to keep track of them</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I've only found the need to do this with Unity and Argent Adept</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ameena\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/48/1907_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ameena:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Also, does anyone playing ever actually have their hand  in their hand ?&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yes, I like holding my cards in hand … in hand. Not trying to be cutesy. I totally understand playing with the cards on the table and visible to all. Generally, though, I enjoy both the visceral feel of holding the cards and the cooperation that comes from relying on the other players to represent what's in their hand. Also, I think holding the cards-in-hand rather than putting them face up on the table reduces a bit the likelihood of confusing which cards are in-hand versus in-play.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
