      {
        "id": 40761,
        "name": "Vyolynce",
        "username": "Vyolynce",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/vyolynce/{size}/2397_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-10-24T12:56:58.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"arenson9\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/48/1900_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> arenson9:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><b> Ameena wrote:</b></p>\n<div><blockquote>Bleh,I move my played cards around so as to keep track of them\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nI've only found the need to do this with Unity and Argent Adept\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yeah arranging Adept's ongoings into like-typed piles saves so much headaches. Of course, none of his cards have effects that fire off in a specific order, so it really doesn't apply to him.</p>",
