      {
        "id": 40768,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-10-24T15:42:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I think I'll just continue playing as I have been, without making things all complicated - it's only a game after all ;).</p><p>On the point of not getting hand-cards confused with in-play cards, I always have the same layout of two rows in front of me. In the row nearest me, on the far left, I have my discard pile. To the right of that, my draw pile. To the right of that, the rest of the row consists of my hand. The second row is parallel to the first. Level with my draw deck is my Hero card, then to the right of that my Ongoings and Equipment in some kind of logical order running left-to-right from there. One-Shots get played in a space usually to the right of the end of the in-play row (if there's room, though there usually is - it's generally my hand that has a zillion cards in it, except for last week when I had about a quarter of the Adept's deck in-play :D) so I can have them separate from my other cards, so as not to get confused as I work through everything that needs doing on the one-shot.</p>",
        "post_number": 29,
